# Claude Code permissions that must exist on EVERY machine.
#
# One `permissions.allow` entry per line. Blank lines and `#` comments ignored.
# `bin/ai-claude-permissions` merges these into the USER-level settings file
# (~/.claude/settings.json), so they cover every project on the machine.
#
# This file is additive only: the script never removes an entry a machine
# already has, and never touches `deny`, `ask`, or anything else in the file.
# Delete a line here and it simply stops being enforced on the next sync;
# machines that already have it keep it.
#
# Browser page-inspection tools. A session doing visual/UI verification needs
# these to screenshot and read a rendered page; without them it stops on a
# permission prompt that nobody is sitting there to answer. Added 2026-08-13.
mcp__playwright__browser_evaluate
mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool

# Read-only commands that 245 sessions in 2026-09/10 stopped on (transcript
# analysis 2026-10-21). Read-only prefixes only. Deliberately NOT here: `find`
# (it has -delete/-exec) and `timeout` (a prefix rule would allow any command
# behind it).
Bash(git status:*)
Bash(git log:*)
Bash(git diff:*)
Bash(git branch --show-current:*)
Bash(git branch -a:*)
Bash(git branch --list:*)
Bash(git show:*)
Bash(gh pr view:*)
Bash(gh pr checks:*)
Bash(gh issue view:*)
Bash(ls:*)
Bash(cat:*)
Bash(grep:*)
Bash(rg:*)
Bash(wc:*)
Bash(head:*)
Bash(tail:*)
